From 822cea6aae1769125d64041e5f64387a13aaa84f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 22:29:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 50/93] demux: rawdv: fix wrong pcr after a seek

Control() is a bare demux_vaControlHelper() call, and the helper implements
DEMUX_SET_POSITION and DEMUX_SET_TIME as a plain vlc_stream_Seek(): the
stream moves, but p_sys->i_pcr is left untouched and keeps counting from
where it was before the seek.

DEMUX_GET_TIME goes through the same helper and is derived from the byte
offset, so it stays correct, and the timestamps the demuxer emits no longer
agree with the time it reports. Playback of the track itself survives
because the input resets the PCR on every seek, but slave ES do not:
SlaveDemux() paces external subtitles from the master DEMUX_GET_TIME, so
after a seek they are shifted by the accumulated error, or dropped for
being too late or too early.

The helper seeks frame aligned, so the new offset gives back the frame
number: derive i_pcr from it, with the frame duration Demux() already uses.
Skipped in hurry up mode, where i_pcr is overwritten with the wall clock on
every Demux() call anyway.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/rawdv.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/rawdv.c b/modules/demux/rawdv.c
index acd98b13f3..94d63b1ef5 100644
--- a/modules/demux/rawdv.c
+++ b/modules/demux/rawdv.c
@@ -307,9 +307,31 @@ static int Control( demux_t *p_demux, int i_query, va_list args )
     demux_sys_t *p_sys  = p_demux->p_sys;
 
     /* XXX: DEMUX_SET_TIME is precise here */
-    return demux_vaControlHelper( p_demux->s,
-                                   0, -1,
-                                   p_sys->frame_size * p_sys->f_rate * 8,
-                                   p_sys->frame_size, i_query, args );
+    int i_ret = demux_vaControlHelper( p_demux->s,
+                                       0, -1,
+                                       p_sys->frame_size * p_sys->f_rate * 8,
+                                       p_sys->frame_size, i_query, args );
+    if( i_ret != VLC_SUCCESS )
+        return i_ret;
+
+    switch( i_query )
+    {
+        case DEMUX_SET_POSITION:
+        case DEMUX_SET_TIME:
+            /* The helper only moved the stream: resync the pcr accumulator,
+             * else it would keep counting from before the seek and drift
+             * away from the byte derived DEMUX_GET_TIME. The helper seeks
+             * frame aligned, so the offset gives back the frame number.
+             * Pointless in hurry up mode, where the pcr is the wall clock. */
+            if( !p_sys->b_hurry_up )
+                p_sys->i_pcr = ( vlc_stream_Tell( p_demux->s )
+                                 / p_sys->frame_size )
+                             * ( INT64_C(1000000) / p_sys->f_rate );
+            break;
+        default:
+            break;
+    }
+
+    return VLC_SUCCESS;
 }
 
